#: ../../../installation.rst:3
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:6
msgid "Install package with pip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:8
msgid "To install with pip::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:10
msgid "$ pip install scikit-build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:13
msgid "Install from source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:15
msgid ""
"To install scikit-build from the latest source, first obtain the source "
"code::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:17
msgid ""
"$ git clone https://github.com/scikit-build/scikit-build\n"
"$ cd scikit-build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:20
msgid "then install with::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:22
msgid "$ pip install ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:24
msgid "or::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:26
msgid "$ pip install -e ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:28
msgid "for development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:32
msgid "Dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:35
msgid "Python Packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:37
msgid ""
"The main runtime dependency is ``scikit-build-core[setuptools]``, which "
"provides the build backend. The full list of dependencies can be seen in "
"``pyproject.toml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:42
msgid "Compiler Toolchain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:44
msgid ""
"The same compiler toolchain used to build the CPython interpreter should "
"also be available. Refer to the `CPython Developer's Guide <https://devguide."
"python.org/getting-started/setup-building/#install-dependencies>`_ for "
"details about the compiler toolchain for your operating system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:49
msgid "For example, on *Ubuntu Linux*, install with::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:51
msgid "$ sudo apt-get install build-essential"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:53
msgid ""
"On *macOS*, install `Xcode <https://developer.apple.com/xcode/>`_ or the "
"command line tools (``xcode-select --install``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:56
msgid ""
"On *Windows*, install `Visual Studio <https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/"
"visual-cpp-build-tools/>`_ with the C++ workload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:63
msgid "CMake"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:65
msgid ""
"The easiest way to get `CMake <https://www.cmake.org/>`_ is :ref:`to add it "
"to the pyproject.toml file <basic_usage_example>`. The CMake Python package "
"is then downloaded and installed when your project is built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:69
msgid "To manually install the *cmake* package from PyPI::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:71
msgid "$ pip install cmake"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:73
msgid "To install the *cmake* package in conda::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:75
msgid "$ conda install -c conda-forge cmake"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:77
msgid ""
"You can also `download the standard CMake binaries <https://cmake.org/"
"download>`_ for your platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../installation.rst:80
msgid ""
"Alternatively, `build CMake from source <https://cmake.org/install/>`_ with "
"a C++ compiler if binaries are not available for your operating system."
msgstr ""
